# What the runtime image's `COPY . /baked` takes from the repository root. `.gitignore` keeps local configuration,
# secrets and machine-specific files out of git, and this list keeps the same files out of the image layer, which is
# what `*.local.*`, `.env` and `.env*.local` cover (an appended deny list, a resolved browser target list, a decrypted
# environment and a local task file all match). The build output and cache trees in the middle are what the mutation
# run never needs and would otherwise copy tens of gigabytes.
.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.cache
**/target
**/output
**/corpus
**/.stryker-tmp
.env
.env*.local
*.local.*
.claude
